WEBVTT

00:32.240 --> 00:36.953
THE PRACTICAL GUIDE TO LOVE

00:41.749 --> 00:43.793
You've had too much to drink.

00:44.335 --> 00:46.712
Let's end the meeting here.

00:46.879 --> 00:48.130
I'll call you another time.

00:50.591 --> 00:53.386
- Where the hell are you going?
- That hurts! Let go!

00:53.469 --> 00:55.012
You think you can just leave?

00:55.096 --> 00:57.181
Let go! It hurts!

01:01.519 --> 01:02.687
Tae-seop!

01:02.895 --> 01:04.105
Who the hell are you?

01:04.188 --> 01:06.315
Me? Her boyfriend.

01:06.399 --> 01:07.400
Huh?

01:09.860 --> 01:11.195
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

01:11.279 --> 01:12.822
Hold up. What did you just say?

01:13.406 --> 01:14.991
You had a boyfriend all along?

01:16.284 --> 01:17.743
Damn it!

01:18.119 --> 01:20.454
Why would he set me up with a woman
who's already taken?

01:21.330 --> 01:22.915
Set you up?

01:24.083 --> 01:25.751
Who set you up with me?

01:28.462 --> 01:29.714
I knew something was off.

01:29.797 --> 01:32.842
I'm not going to let this slide.

01:32.925 --> 01:35.344
Don't even dream
of getting your hands on our products!

01:35.428 --> 01:37.263
Please stop there and leave.

01:37.763 --> 01:40.099
Why do you keep interrupting us?

01:40.182 --> 01:42.518
Better me interrupting than the police.

01:42.810 --> 01:45.646
You've got a lot of eyes watching.
And the CCTV is filming it all.

01:57.658 --> 01:58.868
Damn it!

02:05.499 --> 02:07.084
Good luck getting your damn cattle!

02:08.169 --> 02:10.421
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

02:10.588 --> 02:11.922
Does your wrist hurt a lot? Let me see.

02:13.341 --> 02:14.634
Oh, gosh.

02:15.426 --> 02:16.469
That jerk.

02:18.971 --> 02:20.765
By the way

02:20.848 --> 02:22.850
how did you know to come here?

02:22.933 --> 02:24.060
Oh, well...

02:25.061 --> 02:27.188
Mr. Shin called me.

02:27.772 --> 02:29.690
- Ji-su?
- Yeah.

02:34.945 --> 02:37.615
I keep thinking about someone else.

02:37.698 --> 02:39.950
I promise not to cross the line.

02:40.242 --> 02:42.328
I won't bother you. All good now?

03:12.775 --> 03:14.735
How could I not have realized this?

03:14.819 --> 03:17.113
Don't beat yourself up over it.
You should be mad.

03:19.699 --> 03:21.575
Let's go. I'll drive you home.

03:38.467 --> 03:43.139
THE PRACTICAL GUIDE TO LOVE
EPISODE 10

03:43.973 --> 03:47.226
Mr. Oh seems to have set you up
for that meeting because it was a date.

03:47.393 --> 03:50.396
From what you've told me,
it seems like the guy knew it was a date.

03:51.814 --> 03:54.483
- Touch it.
- What? No, thanks.

03:54.567 --> 03:55.985
You're old enough to know everything.

03:56.068 --> 03:59.947
It's not fun
when a woman keeps acting so innocent.

04:00.030 --> 04:01.866
So, how many men have you dated?

04:01.949 --> 04:03.451
Three? Four?

04:05.077 --> 04:07.163
But why would Mr. Oh do that?

04:07.246 --> 04:08.831
He must've wanted to make this happen

04:08.914 --> 04:10.875
knowing how keen
the Senior Managing Director was.

04:10.958 --> 04:13.627
He probably didn't think
anything would go wrong over one dinner.

04:13.753 --> 04:16.589
I know you've gone
on a lot of blind dates lately.

04:16.672 --> 04:17.923
But as you know

04:18.007 --> 04:20.843
blind dates are good experience,
even if things don't work out.

04:20.968 --> 04:23.179
And sometimes, you get lucky
and find a good one.

04:23.304 --> 04:24.305
Take the card.

04:24.805 --> 04:28.100
Order whatever you want with it, okay?

04:31.812 --> 04:35.858
How could he do this?
It was a work meeting.

04:35.941 --> 04:38.861
I can't let this slide, either.

04:38.944 --> 04:40.946
He totally undermined us.

04:41.113 --> 04:43.532
I'll file a formal complaint
with the hotel.

04:57.087 --> 04:58.714
LIVESTOCK ENVIRONMENT MANAGEMENT AGENCY

05:00.049 --> 05:01.050
WHAT'S GOING ON IN THE CONFERENCE ROOM?

05:02.551 --> 05:03.636
IS SOMETHING WRONG AT PURCHASING?

05:03.719 --> 05:04.845
I HEAR MR. OH HAD A BIG FIGHT
WITH HIS TEAMMATES

05:05.638 --> 05:07.515
Why are they getting so nosy
about nothing?

05:08.724 --> 05:10.976
As if it's not bad enough already.

05:35.417 --> 05:36.502
How did it go?

05:37.127 --> 05:39.630
I just recounted everything that happened

05:39.797 --> 05:42.132
from the sudden change
in the project manager

05:42.258 --> 05:44.260
to the things that happened to Ui-yeong.

05:44.885 --> 05:48.514
Mr. Oh is having a meeting
with the Grievance Committee.

05:49.473 --> 05:51.475
OFFICE AUTOMATION ROOM

05:51.559 --> 05:53.269
Let's get some coffee.

06:24.091 --> 06:26.218
- Ui-yeong.
- Mr. Oh.

06:28.721 --> 06:29.763
Well...

06:30.931 --> 06:31.932
I'm sorry.

06:32.850 --> 06:35.227
I thought it'd make things easier

06:36.020 --> 06:39.773
if the people working on the project
got along...

06:41.942 --> 06:44.278
No, I have no excuse.

06:46.030 --> 06:47.781
I'm really sorry this time.

06:49.450 --> 06:50.910
This won't ever happen again.

06:52.620 --> 06:53.787
I promise you that.

06:54.830 --> 06:56.248
Okay.

06:57.291 --> 06:58.375
Sorry.

07:23.859 --> 07:26.236
Ui-yeong,
you haven't had lunch yet, right?

07:36.372 --> 07:38.040
We'll take two of the chef's specials.

07:38.123 --> 07:40.417
- Okay, I'll get that ready right away.
- Thank you.

07:42.127 --> 07:43.128
Well...

07:43.587 --> 07:46.215
I should've at least changed
out of my uniform.

07:47.174 --> 07:48.968
It's fine.

07:49.051 --> 07:51.220
We're here as guests.

07:51.637 --> 07:54.556
And the hotel doesn't own this place.
It's an outside vendor.

07:54.640 --> 07:56.225
We don't even get employee discounts.

07:56.308 --> 07:59.728
Don't be shy and enjoy it all.

08:07.361 --> 08:09.196
This is such a fancy lunch.

08:09.279 --> 08:12.574
You need to enjoy something good
to make yourself feel better.

08:12.741 --> 08:13.784
Dig in.

08:15.077 --> 08:17.204
Sorry for not appreciating you
as our key employee

08:17.287 --> 08:21.667
when we were prioritizing the hotel
over you.

08:21.750 --> 08:22.835
It's okay.

08:25.004 --> 08:26.630
Mr. Oh apologized

08:27.214 --> 08:29.133
and you've gone so far
to make me feel better.

08:29.508 --> 08:32.386
I don't think I'll remember this
as being that bad.

08:36.724 --> 08:40.436
You've been working at our hotel
for about ten years now, right?

08:42.104 --> 08:43.105
Yeah.

08:44.023 --> 08:49.069
You'll get burnt out at the hotel
if you let something like this slide.

08:49.528 --> 08:53.198
So, until the Disciplinary Committee
decides what to do with Mr. Oh

08:54.033 --> 08:57.494
we want to give you a few days off.

08:58.245 --> 08:59.455
A few days off?

09:00.581 --> 09:05.127
But I have a lot on my plate right now.
I need to look for another producer, too.

09:05.794 --> 09:08.297
Oh, I thought you'd be excited.

09:09.506 --> 09:12.134
Come to think of it,
you haven't had a proper vacation yet.

09:12.217 --> 09:14.803
You also went straight through college
without a break.

09:15.763 --> 09:17.765
- Yeah.
- As admirable as that is

09:18.640 --> 09:20.559
sometimes, I feel bad for you.

09:22.352 --> 09:25.314
Na-ri's determined to do well now,
so don't worry.

09:25.731 --> 09:27.900
Why don't you take this chance

09:27.983 --> 09:31.737
to take some time for yourself?

09:36.492 --> 09:38.577
Okay, I will.

09:39.161 --> 09:41.580
Okay, keep eating. It's good soup.

09:41.663 --> 09:43.373
Okay, thank you.

09:53.759 --> 09:56.845
- Hey, Mom.
- What are you doing? Don't you have work?

09:57.179 --> 09:58.931
Oh, I got a few days off.

09:59.389 --> 10:01.433
But my body still thinks
it's time for work.

10:01.767 --> 10:02.851
That's random.

10:03.685 --> 10:04.853
Did you do something wrong?

10:04.937 --> 10:06.396
No, I was wronged...

10:06.605 --> 10:09.399
No, they just told me
to get some rest and recharge.

10:10.317 --> 10:12.736
Didn't I tell you to stand your ground

10:12.820 --> 10:15.781
to keep people from undermining you?

10:16.240 --> 10:18.033
Nobody undermines me as much as you do.

10:18.117 --> 10:20.661
Stop nagging. Just get to work.

10:21.745 --> 10:22.996
Clean the house.

10:23.455 --> 10:25.582
- You don't get a day off from chores.
- My gosh.

10:26.083 --> 10:27.334
What's your plan now?

10:27.417 --> 10:29.128
Don't worry. I have plenty to do!

10:29.211 --> 10:31.004
- Just go!
- Okay, bye.

10:31.088 --> 10:32.798
- Have a good day.
- Bye.

10:34.591 --> 10:35.592
What should I do now?

10:40.556 --> 10:44.059
There's nothing to do.
Can't believe I came to the gym myself.

10:45.435 --> 10:47.896
I just started,
and I'm already getting flooded with work.

10:48.522 --> 10:51.108
Oh, no.
Maybe this will make you feel better.

10:51.191 --> 10:53.026
OH, NO.
MAYBE THIS WILL MAKE YOU FEEL BETTER

10:56.363 --> 10:58.323
I'll need to see your forearms
to feel better.

11:03.412 --> 11:05.539
Take a photo of your face or your arms,
not both.

11:05.789 --> 11:08.208
You think you can make both look good
in one photo?

11:14.381 --> 11:19.178
I'LL NEED TO SEE YOUR FOREARMS
TO FEEL BETTER

11:19.803 --> 11:21.054
I definitely feel better now!

11:29.646 --> 11:32.316
Hyun-min, any updates on the market visit?

11:32.441 --> 11:33.609
No, nothing.

11:33.692 --> 11:36.361
But the reporter who wrote
about tiger cattle replied

11:36.445 --> 11:38.780
so I'll ask her
about the farm in the article.

11:38.864 --> 11:39.865
From a reporter?

11:40.240 --> 11:42.492
Hold on. Why is everyone reading the chat?

11:43.243 --> 11:45.120
Ui-yeong, you're reading the chat!

11:45.579 --> 11:47.539
Let's leave this chat and start a new one.

11:47.664 --> 11:49.291
No, wait!

11:49.666 --> 11:51.168
Come on.

11:51.293 --> 11:54.254
You can work or rest, but not both.

11:54.880 --> 11:57.299
I'll have to take care of all of it
once I'm back, anyway.

11:58.175 --> 12:02.137
Come on. You know things you've been
putting off because you've been busy.

12:02.721 --> 12:04.223
Do those, one by one.

12:07.851 --> 12:10.646
Hey, how come you're not making me
do squats or lunges

12:10.729 --> 12:13.023
when you're not the one on vacation
right now?

12:13.148 --> 12:15.400
Alright, get into the plank pose
right now.

12:16.485 --> 12:18.737
You're lying facing up?
Let's do leg raises.

12:18.946 --> 12:21.531
To the side? Let's work your obliques.

12:21.615 --> 12:23.575
Tighten your core muscles!

12:23.659 --> 12:25.786
WISHLIST: A RELAXED MORNING, READING,
SPENDING TIME WITH MOM, TRYING A NEW THING

12:25.869 --> 12:28.872
I've been putting off tons of things
because I haven't had time.

12:37.673 --> 12:38.674
Oh!

12:40.926 --> 12:42.177
A DATE WITH TAE-SEOP

12:42.302 --> 12:43.303
A date.

12:47.432 --> 12:48.433
What else?

12:48.517 --> 12:50.686
- See you.
- No, wait!

12:51.520 --> 12:52.938
Ta-da! It's for you.

12:53.605 --> 12:54.690
What?

12:55.524 --> 12:56.733
- Thanks.
- You're welcome.

12:56.817 --> 12:58.527
- Have a good day!
- Bye!

13:09.913 --> 13:11.081
It smells so nice.

13:20.549 --> 13:24.303
ENJOYING A RELAXING MORNING, CHECK

13:28.849 --> 13:32.477
READING A BOOK, CHECK

13:40.861 --> 13:42.779
I don't like things that hurt.

13:43.071 --> 13:46.033
My colleague is scared of everything

13:46.283 --> 13:47.659
and she said this was painless.

13:47.909 --> 13:49.703
It's about time you got some work done.

13:50.537 --> 13:52.914
If it's so good, why don't you get it?

13:52.998 --> 13:55.500
Let me be a good daughter for once,
alright?

14:03.383 --> 14:05.635
You can sleep if you get sleepy.

14:05.927 --> 14:07.012
Okay.

14:09.431 --> 14:11.266
How is it? Do you like it?

14:15.771 --> 14:20.025
DOING A FULL-BODY STRETCH, CHECK

14:20.108 --> 14:22.736
- Slowly!
- Here we go!

14:24.905 --> 14:25.989
Stop it!

14:26.073 --> 14:27.783
You're so stiff.

14:28.617 --> 14:29.618
That hurts.

14:30.077 --> 14:31.244
Go like this.

14:35.749 --> 14:37.376
PARK JEONG-IM

14:38.752 --> 14:39.878
Hello.

14:40.962 --> 14:42.089
- Jeong-im.
- Yeah?

14:42.172 --> 14:44.216
Why don't you eat lunch with us
these days?

14:44.424 --> 14:47.219
My daughter's on vacation

14:47.302 --> 14:49.304
and I guess
she likes making breakfast now.

14:50.180 --> 14:51.973
She made me lunch, so I had this instead.

14:52.307 --> 14:54.184
She makes lunches for you
while on vacation?

14:54.393 --> 14:56.144
What a kind daughter you have!

14:56.228 --> 14:59.022
You wouldn't be saying that
if you'd actually tasted it.

15:00.190 --> 15:01.691
Did you schedule your physical?

15:01.858 --> 15:03.110
Oh, right.

15:04.194 --> 15:05.987
You want to go with me this year, too?

15:07.531 --> 15:09.366
I don't mean to show off

15:09.616 --> 15:12.327
but my son asked me first,
so I've already booked an appointment.

15:12.411 --> 15:14.079
We're going to an all-you-can-eat, too!

15:14.162 --> 15:16.289
- That'll be a nice date.
- Yeah.

15:16.373 --> 15:18.834
You should go with your daughter, too.

15:18.917 --> 15:20.585
She'll keep you company.

15:20.669 --> 15:23.839
Me? No, I'll just go by myself.

15:24.005 --> 15:28.218
I don't know what she's doing,
but she seems so busy.

15:32.722 --> 15:34.099
Am I painting this?

15:34.182 --> 15:35.851
- Yeah.
- What if I ruin it?

15:36.685 --> 15:38.145
It's okay, I'll show you.

15:39.521 --> 15:41.022
Watch what I do.

15:42.983 --> 15:46.027
Just spread it evenly, like this.

15:46.736 --> 15:48.238
- Here.
- That sounds fun.

15:48.905 --> 15:51.616
Hold on. You should tie your hair.

15:53.285 --> 15:55.078
Let me do it for you.

15:57.289 --> 15:58.623
You know how to tie hair?

15:58.707 --> 15:59.708
No.

16:01.084 --> 16:02.085
Like this.

16:03.378 --> 16:04.379
Go!

16:05.297 --> 16:06.339
All good now.

16:08.175 --> 16:09.551
- Here I go.
- Okay.

16:10.010 --> 16:11.178
Get some of this...

16:17.559 --> 16:19.019
Yes, just spread that.

16:20.937 --> 16:21.938
You're doing great.

16:22.772 --> 16:24.274
I think I'm better than you.

16:24.357 --> 16:25.442
TRYING SOMETHING NEW, CHECK
A DATE WITH TAE-SEOP, CHECK

16:25.525 --> 16:27.360
- You're talented.
- This is fun.

16:28.195 --> 16:30.489
You're really getting the hang
of this vacation thing.

16:30.655 --> 16:32.324
You're not talking about work at all.

16:32.532 --> 16:34.910
I have no time to think about work
when I'm so busy.

16:34.993 --> 16:38.330
Woodworking is like meditation.

16:38.622 --> 16:40.790
You stop overthinking
when you get in the zone.

16:41.374 --> 16:43.043
- I get it.
- Right?

16:43.960 --> 16:45.170
You're so good.

16:45.253 --> 16:47.422
- I think I'm actually talented.
- Yeah.

16:50.133 --> 16:53.261
You just need to keep it somewhere cool
to dry for 24 hours.

16:53.345 --> 16:54.387
I see.

17:01.144 --> 17:02.562
I have something to show you.

17:03.271 --> 17:04.898
- What?
- Ta-da!

17:06.149 --> 17:07.234
It's a photo!

17:09.653 --> 17:14.449
I'll trade this for the baby photo of you
I said I wanted.

17:14.699 --> 17:15.700
Okay.

17:16.493 --> 17:19.162
You were beautiful, even as a kid.

17:19.996 --> 17:21.957
Were you on a trip to the beach?

17:22.290 --> 17:25.377
Yeah, I was about seven or eight.

17:25.460 --> 17:28.421
This was from a summer trip
with my parents.

17:29.464 --> 17:33.051
This was probably the last family trip
we took together.

17:35.428 --> 17:37.305
I remember it feeling...

17:37.389 --> 17:41.518
so warm and wonderful.

17:42.102 --> 17:45.605
But I don't remember anything
aside from feeling that way in the moment.

17:46.231 --> 17:49.317
Because you don't realize
it's a special moment when you're a kid.

17:49.401 --> 17:50.485
I know.

17:50.569 --> 17:54.239
I would've cherished such a moment
if I were to have it now.

17:55.031 --> 17:57.284
I wouldn't even forget it,
even if someone told me to.

17:59.452 --> 18:00.495
Like right now.

18:01.663 --> 18:03.540
- Right now?
- Yeah.

18:04.666 --> 18:06.418
When would I ever get a spontaneous break

18:06.543 --> 18:08.712
and spend time with you like this

18:08.795 --> 18:12.966
under the excuse of trying something new?

18:13.049 --> 18:16.303
You're right. This is really precious.

18:16.386 --> 18:17.804
I know.

18:22.976 --> 18:24.102
Don't I look better now?

18:25.270 --> 18:27.522
- I don't think so.
- So mean!

18:47.167 --> 18:48.960
Oh, gosh! What?

18:49.294 --> 18:51.671
I e-mailed and texted you
yesterday and today

18:51.755 --> 18:53.423
but you didn't reply, so here I am.

18:54.591 --> 18:55.675
Check it out.

18:57.719 --> 18:59.387
Sorry!

18:59.929 --> 19:04.100
I've just been all over the place.

19:04.768 --> 19:07.062
But the contract's about to be signed

19:07.145 --> 19:10.231
and the gift set is coming along nicely.

19:11.858 --> 19:14.152
Hold on tight. It's the weekend soon.

19:15.153 --> 19:16.154
Thanks.

19:16.571 --> 19:19.282
Yeah, it's almost the weekend.

19:19.366 --> 19:21.284
Hello, Chef.

19:25.163 --> 19:26.247
Hyun-min.

19:27.040 --> 19:28.041
What?

19:28.249 --> 19:31.503
You'll need to visit the cattle farm
this weekend.

19:32.045 --> 19:33.046
What?

19:34.297 --> 19:36.549
Sorry, there's just not enough time.

19:36.716 --> 19:39.761
Just do a site visit
and get the contract signed.

19:40.011 --> 19:41.346
Na-ri!

19:42.055 --> 19:44.766
How can you steal my weekend from me?

19:46.685 --> 19:48.269
It's not like I get to rest, either!

19:48.395 --> 19:50.730
I'll take care of everything else

19:50.980 --> 19:52.565
so just take care of the farm for me.

19:53.274 --> 19:54.401
Alright...

19:57.904 --> 19:59.114
Ui-yeong!

20:00.240 --> 20:01.616
I miss you.

20:04.744 --> 20:06.037
- Ui-yeong!
- Oh!

20:06.955 --> 20:09.791
Ui-yeong!

20:09.874 --> 20:10.917
How have you been?

20:11.751 --> 20:14.254
How are you? I missed you!

20:14.379 --> 20:15.797
It's only been a few days.

20:16.047 --> 20:18.258
It's like I lost my youth
the moment you left.

20:18.383 --> 20:20.468
I realized how precious you were
once you left.

20:21.511 --> 20:25.140
Let's go.
I chose the best restaurant for you!

20:25.223 --> 20:26.891
I can't wait! Let's head in.

20:28.852 --> 20:30.603
Let's go.

20:31.479 --> 20:33.356
The portion size is huge!

20:33.648 --> 20:35.817
- Thanks.
- Enjoy!

20:44.451 --> 20:46.077
- It's so good.
- Right?

20:46.161 --> 20:47.495
I told you it was good.

20:50.999 --> 20:54.669
Did you really want to see me
just to grab dinner together?

20:55.879 --> 20:58.590
The office feels so empty without you.

20:59.382 --> 21:03.428
All I do is work when I'm not sleeping.

21:03.511 --> 21:05.889
I don't even have time to see
my new boyfriend.

21:06.806 --> 21:09.267
Na-ri told me to visit the cattle farm
for a site visit

21:09.350 --> 21:11.227
and to sign the contract over the weekend.

21:12.103 --> 21:14.272
But I've never signed a contract alone

21:14.355 --> 21:16.065
so I wanted to ask you a few questions.

21:16.357 --> 21:17.442
Where's the farm?

21:17.525 --> 21:19.402
Sokcho, Gangwon-do.

21:19.819 --> 21:20.904
Sokcho...

21:22.363 --> 21:23.573
You want me to go with you?

21:25.241 --> 21:26.326
Really?

21:26.409 --> 21:28.286
You're treating me to a good dinner

21:28.453 --> 21:30.538
and I might as well make a trip out of it.

21:31.289 --> 21:34.083
I'd love to have you join me!

21:34.209 --> 21:37.712
I'll book our hotel and buses.

21:37.879 --> 21:38.880
Just bring yourself.

21:38.963 --> 21:41.549
And I won't bother you in our free time.

21:41.633 --> 21:43.092
Okay, let's go together.

21:43.551 --> 21:45.345
You're an angel!

21:46.179 --> 21:47.597
- Eat up!
- Okay.

21:48.848 --> 21:50.475
I'm home.

21:51.142 --> 21:52.393
Where were you?

21:52.477 --> 21:54.229
I had dinner with a coworker.

21:54.479 --> 21:55.522
I see.

21:56.231 --> 21:58.358
Are you getting a physical?

21:58.900 --> 22:00.109
Yeah.

22:01.444 --> 22:05.031
You want to watch a movie
if you're free this weekend?

22:05.365 --> 22:06.866
No, I can't.

22:06.991 --> 22:09.410
I need to go to Sokcho to sign a contract.

22:09.619 --> 22:11.955
My colleague's too scared to do it alone.

22:13.206 --> 22:14.749
On your last weekend off?

22:16.000 --> 22:18.253
That should get you ready for Monday,
at least.

22:18.670 --> 22:19.838
I guess so.

22:20.797 --> 22:23.258
I can't believe my vacation's ending.

22:29.180 --> 22:35.478
HKUH CENTER FOR CANCER RESEARCH
DONATION AWARDING CEREMONY

22:36.354 --> 22:39.274
You'll hand out the certificates
to the big donors

22:39.357 --> 22:42.652
and take photos with them,
which will be published in an article.

22:42.735 --> 22:45.822
I think
you left my wife off the guest list.

22:45.905 --> 22:48.241
Did she not tell you?

22:48.324 --> 22:51.077
She called and said
she'd donate the amount she promised

22:51.160 --> 22:53.371
but would not be attending the event.

22:55.123 --> 22:56.165
I see.

22:59.335 --> 23:01.170
- Okay, then.
- Okay.

23:01.254 --> 23:06.384
HKUH CENTER FOR CANCER RESEARCH
DONATION AWARDING CEREMONY

23:12.098 --> 23:13.933
The caller is unavailable.

23:14.100 --> 23:17.353
Please record your message after the beep.

23:21.316 --> 23:25.194
CALL HISTORY

23:28.907 --> 23:32.410
At least I know she's being selective
about who to answer.

23:34.913 --> 23:35.955
Come in.

23:41.920 --> 23:43.004
You can leave it.

23:56.059 --> 23:57.185
SEOUL FAMILY COURT

24:09.030 --> 24:12.742
SEOUL FAMILY COURT

24:15.036 --> 24:17.580
COMPLAINT FILED BY SON JEONG-A
AGAINST SHIN JI-HUN

24:23.461 --> 24:25.129
- Thank you.
- Come again.

24:27.757 --> 24:28.800
Sorry.

24:31.302 --> 24:32.345
Hello.

24:34.013 --> 24:35.473
- Ji-su!
- Yeah?

24:40.478 --> 24:43.272
I've been a fan of yours forever.

24:43.564 --> 24:46.693
- Could I have your autograph?
- Of course. What's your name?

24:47.151 --> 24:49.278
It's Song Cheol.

24:50.363 --> 24:54.492
Please write "For Cheol"
and today's date, too.

24:55.994 --> 24:57.078
Thank you!

24:57.578 --> 24:59.956
You can drink and eat whatever you want.

25:00.164 --> 25:02.500
Ji-su, don't let her pay, okay?

25:09.340 --> 25:11.801
I'll take one hand-drip coffee. Hot.

25:19.392 --> 25:21.477
Don't you have other cafes in Seoul
you can go to?

25:22.645 --> 25:24.814
What happened to doing your best
to avoid me?

25:25.815 --> 25:27.150
I came to tell you something.

25:27.859 --> 25:29.444
It wasn't anything to text you about.

25:31.904 --> 25:33.322
I'm not interested.

25:34.699 --> 25:35.783
You're so cold.

25:35.992 --> 25:38.870
I'm getting a divorce.

25:39.412 --> 25:40.413
What?

25:49.464 --> 25:50.590
Are you serious?

25:51.674 --> 25:54.135
You seem quite shaken
for someone who isn't interested.

25:55.344 --> 25:56.846
We're processing it quietly.

25:57.930 --> 25:59.807
You acted like Romeo and Juliet.

26:01.768 --> 26:03.311
And it's over, just like that?

26:04.187 --> 26:06.856
I didn't expect a disappointing ending
when I fell in love.

26:07.648 --> 26:08.941
But I recently found out

26:10.401 --> 26:12.570
that he lied to get with me.

26:14.072 --> 26:16.407
I checked your mother's medical record
with my own eyes.

26:18.618 --> 26:21.412
He was seeing me
while she was undergoing chemo.

26:24.707 --> 26:25.875
I had no idea.

26:27.710 --> 26:28.711
No

26:29.629 --> 26:31.255
maybe I just let myself be blinded.

26:32.048 --> 26:33.841
When you're deeply in love

26:33.925 --> 26:37.720
you want to reject the truth,
no matter how desperately it knocks.

26:37.929 --> 26:41.349
Love that makes you numb
to someone else's pain.

26:41.557 --> 26:42.767
Isn't it disgusting?

26:44.477 --> 26:45.478
But...

26:47.021 --> 26:49.065
the truth feels so important now.

26:52.193 --> 26:53.277
I'm sorry.

26:53.778 --> 26:54.821
After all that?

26:55.947 --> 26:57.281
I'm sorry it took me so long.

26:58.574 --> 26:59.867
I'm really sorry.

27:01.119 --> 27:02.245
I mean it.

27:21.681 --> 27:23.683
- Hello, Director.
- Hello.

27:24.934 --> 27:25.935
- Hello.
- Hello.

27:26.018 --> 27:28.437
- Hello.
- Hello.

27:30.815 --> 27:31.941
Hello, Director.

27:36.070 --> 27:37.113
- Hey.
- Yeah?

27:37.196 --> 27:38.698
You really sure about his outfit?

27:39.448 --> 27:41.284
He looks like a model,
not a new detective.

27:42.076 --> 27:45.288
I'll ask the stylist to make
his hair and outfit look more natural.

27:47.206 --> 27:48.958
Go to the dressing room in ten.

27:49.208 --> 27:50.209
Okay.

27:53.880 --> 27:57.133
So, you're the one who got hired
because of Jeong-a.

27:57.925 --> 27:58.968
Sorry?

27:59.135 --> 28:02.763
I hear she's considering another project
over this director's.

28:04.056 --> 28:06.434
Oh, she got you a role
before she ditched him!

28:06.517 --> 28:08.269
No wonder the director's bitter.

28:10.897 --> 28:12.064
But he's handsome.

28:13.566 --> 28:16.444
Are you leaving on Saturday
and returning on Sunday?

28:17.028 --> 28:20.323
Yeah, I'll just visit the farm
and travel around the area.

28:20.531 --> 28:24.785
Oh, the beach in the photo I gave you is
in Sokcho.

28:24.869 --> 28:26.537
I want to go since it's been so long.

28:26.662 --> 28:27.747
I see.

28:28.539 --> 28:30.249
Why don't I tag along?

28:31.167 --> 28:32.210
You?

28:32.293 --> 28:34.378
You have to get back to work soon

28:34.462 --> 28:36.714
so it'll be nice to go on a trip,
even if it's short.

28:36.964 --> 28:39.634
Or would I be a nuisance?

28:41.385 --> 28:42.386
SONG TAE-SEOP

28:43.554 --> 28:45.473
Oh, no.

28:45.681 --> 28:47.433
We're hanging out after work, anyway.

28:47.516 --> 28:49.018
I'll go when you're done.

28:49.477 --> 28:51.646
Let's go to the beach, eat some good food

28:51.729 --> 28:53.189
and I'll drive you back on Sunday.

28:53.272 --> 28:54.273
Sounds good.

28:55.066 --> 28:56.067
This is exciting.

28:57.276 --> 28:58.736
- Okay.
- Bye.

29:04.283 --> 29:06.118
Our first overnight trip?

29:10.790 --> 29:12.416
Mom! I'm heading out.

29:12.500 --> 29:13.793
Oh, okay.

29:13.918 --> 29:15.503
It's an overnight trip, right?

29:15.753 --> 29:18.422
Yeah, don't skip your meals.

29:18.714 --> 29:20.675
And it's okay to see a movie alone, too.

29:20.967 --> 29:22.927
Alright, get going.

29:23.010 --> 29:25.096
- Okay, bye!
- Bye.

29:30.101 --> 29:32.061
Ui-yeong!

29:32.144 --> 29:33.145
Hey.

29:36.023 --> 29:37.817
Thanks so much for tagging along.

29:37.900 --> 29:41.654
It's nothing.
It'll be nice to go to the beach and all.

29:42.321 --> 29:44.657
Alright, it's a trip, then! Let's go!

29:44.740 --> 29:45.741
Let's go!

29:51.038 --> 29:54.333
- They're tiger cattle from Gangwon-do.
- I see.

29:54.417 --> 29:56.252
The meat is very firm and juicy.

29:56.335 --> 29:59.672
Look at them.
They're different from regular cows.

29:59.839 --> 30:01.340
You see the dark ones?

30:01.424 --> 30:03.342
They're different from the other cows.

30:03.718 --> 30:06.345
- Look at that one.
- Yeah.

30:06.429 --> 30:07.972
LICENSE FOR
LIVESTOCK ARTIFICIAL INSEMINATION

30:09.557 --> 30:11.392
PATENT, PRODUCT REGISTRATION CERTIFICATE

30:15.229 --> 30:16.647
You can read it one last time

30:16.731 --> 30:18.607
- and sign it if it's okay.
- Okay.

30:22.611 --> 30:24.697
- What are you doing?
- Hey.

30:25.448 --> 30:27.700
He's my son. He helps me with the farm.

30:27.867 --> 30:29.160
They're from the hotel.

30:31.579 --> 30:32.621
Hello.

30:33.456 --> 30:38.377
My father is a very hardworking farmer.
I look forward to working with you.

30:38.461 --> 30:40.212
We'll do our best, too.

30:40.296 --> 30:41.672
Thank you.

30:46.510 --> 30:48.888
HANKUK UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

30:53.100 --> 30:54.977
You must be tired.

30:55.811 --> 30:58.689
I'm exhausted.

30:58.773 --> 31:00.274
Oh, no.

31:00.691 --> 31:01.984
What should we eat after?

31:02.068 --> 31:04.445
- Maybe chueotang?
- Sounds good.

31:05.821 --> 31:07.031
It was so good last time.

31:07.114 --> 31:08.532
- I know.
- Ms. Park Jeong-im.

31:08.783 --> 31:11.327
- Yes.
- Please head to the MRI room.

31:11.410 --> 31:12.411
Okay.

31:14.330 --> 31:18.292
The two suites are far from each other.
Is that okay?

31:18.417 --> 31:22.171
There are two twin rooms
that are close to each other.

31:22.838 --> 31:26.258
It's okay. Double suites are better.

31:26.342 --> 31:28.886
Of course, we can text each other
if we need.

31:28.969 --> 31:30.304
The bigger the bed, the better.

31:30.846 --> 31:32.723
- Yeah.
- Okay, I'll give you the keys.

31:34.809 --> 31:36.060
- Here.
- Thank you.

31:36.143 --> 31:37.520
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

31:40.981 --> 31:43.109
What do you want to do for dinner?

31:43.567 --> 31:45.111
If you're okay...

31:45.403 --> 31:50.116
Don't mind me at all.
You can enjoy your alone time.

31:51.492 --> 31:52.576
Sure, then.

32:08.092 --> 32:09.427
Tae-seop!

32:09.677 --> 32:10.678
Hey, Ui-yeong.

32:13.472 --> 32:15.766
- Let's go to the beach first.
- Sounds good!

32:23.399 --> 32:26.110
- In the pool? I'll get you a floatie.
- Yeah.

32:30.239 --> 32:31.323
It's stunning.

32:56.223 --> 32:58.142
It looks like a snow-covered mountain.

32:58.225 --> 32:59.768
Yeah, it looks like a mountain.

32:59.977 --> 33:01.061
With snow on top.

33:01.270 --> 33:02.271
I hear something!

33:03.272 --> 33:04.273
Check it out!

33:08.903 --> 33:09.904
Ui-yeong!

33:42.228 --> 33:44.021
This is just the best.

33:44.104 --> 33:46.649
Does the beach look the same as it did
when you were a kid?

33:50.110 --> 33:51.612
I don't think anything's changed.

33:52.905 --> 33:54.532
I guess the ocean doesn't age.

33:55.533 --> 33:56.534
I guess not.

33:57.159 --> 34:00.496
Maybe that's why I feel so calm
when I look at the ocean.

34:02.581 --> 34:05.209
Your feet are covered in sand now.

34:05.292 --> 34:07.336
It's fine. I can dust it off.

34:10.130 --> 34:11.799
This is what I love about you.

34:11.882 --> 34:13.175
Hmm? What?

34:14.552 --> 34:16.720
When you take a dog on a walk

34:17.137 --> 34:19.890
you see them running
to their favorite things

34:20.015 --> 34:22.726
regardless of their feet
getting wet or dirty.

34:23.352 --> 34:25.437
That's the loveliest thing about them.

34:26.605 --> 34:29.024
Aud you're the same.

34:31.110 --> 34:33.737
And I love this about you.

34:34.071 --> 34:35.114
Hmm?

34:36.031 --> 34:39.994
You find every little thing about me
so cute and lovable.

34:41.370 --> 34:46.000
That makes me want to show you
more of myself.

34:48.586 --> 34:49.587
I love that.

35:05.060 --> 35:08.647
The farmer recommended
a sashimi restaurant. You want to go?

35:08.814 --> 35:09.898
Sounds good.

35:10.357 --> 35:13.235
Is Hyun-min not having dinner?

35:13.527 --> 35:15.613
Maybe she's sleeping.
She hasn't checked my texts.

35:15.738 --> 35:16.739
What?

35:18.657 --> 35:19.825
Here.

35:20.492 --> 35:21.577
That was fun.

35:25.539 --> 35:29.084
YEONGGEUM SEAFOOD

35:39.970 --> 35:42.306
Sorry! We're closed for the day.

35:42.389 --> 35:45.184
-Sorry?
- We have a 100-group limit. Try tomorrow.

35:45.267 --> 35:47.603
Oh, no, we came from far away, though.

35:47.686 --> 35:48.979
We're heading back tomorrow.

35:49.688 --> 35:51.023
Sorry about that.

35:54.568 --> 35:55.944
This is so sad.

35:56.028 --> 35:59.323
Should we look for another spot?
I saw a lot of seafood restaurants around.

35:59.406 --> 36:01.408
We have no choice. Let's go.

36:05.954 --> 36:06.955
Oh?

36:07.498 --> 36:09.124
- Why?
- Tae-seop

36:10.209 --> 36:11.669
it looks like we can eat here.

36:14.046 --> 36:15.047
Oh!

36:20.177 --> 36:22.846
- Ah!
- Ah!

36:24.264 --> 36:25.683
- Ui-yeong!
- Look at that.

36:25.766 --> 36:28.894
I thought you were sleeping,
but you were sneaking your guy along!

36:30.729 --> 36:34.108
I don't think I'm the only one
killing two birds with one stone here.

36:34.358 --> 36:37.277
That explains what you said
when we were checking in...

36:37.361 --> 36:38.862
The bed...

36:41.156 --> 36:42.157
Wait!

36:42.491 --> 36:45.786
So, my Min is colleagues with Ui-yeong?

36:45.869 --> 36:48.664
Yeah, Jun, how do you know Ui-yeong?

36:49.331 --> 36:51.834
"Min" and "Jun"? My gosh.

36:53.585 --> 36:56.088
I helped you two save your relationship.

36:58.132 --> 37:00.008
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

37:05.264 --> 37:08.058
- So, you were Choco Killer.
- Yeah.

37:09.768 --> 37:12.229
Let me make you a ssam to thank you.

37:12.521 --> 37:15.733
No need for that.
Please just get along. Don't fight.

37:15.816 --> 37:18.569
Even if you fight, don't call me, okay?

37:19.069 --> 37:20.612
We'll make sure that doesn't happen.

37:21.530 --> 37:23.031
- Ah!
- Ah.

37:23.407 --> 37:24.491
What a cutie!

37:25.576 --> 37:28.454
So, you knew each other for years, right?

37:28.537 --> 37:30.289
How was my Jun in college?

37:30.372 --> 37:33.250
Was he super popular?
Did he have fan girls following him?

37:35.294 --> 37:38.422
I know he looks like a human now

37:38.505 --> 37:42.634
but you wouldn't have wanted to date him
if you'd met him college, either.

37:45.095 --> 37:46.430
Excuse me.

37:46.638 --> 37:49.016
- You were a total loser, too!
- Hey!

37:50.142 --> 37:53.270
But Ui-yeong was so smart in school.

37:53.353 --> 37:56.315
She knew how to find seats at the library,
get cheap coffee

37:56.565 --> 37:59.067
and even sign up for a savings account
for a house.

37:59.151 --> 38:02.112
We were basically friends for survival.

38:02.196 --> 38:03.197
That's right.

38:03.489 --> 38:06.533
I knew Ui-yeong was always smart!

38:07.159 --> 38:11.955
My Jun! You were such a good friend!
What a cutie.

38:12.206 --> 38:14.124
You're a cutie, too, my Min.

38:15.292 --> 38:17.044
Here's your favorite, Min.

38:17.503 --> 38:20.506
- Say ah!
- Ah!

38:20.589 --> 38:22.674
YEONGGEUM SEAFOOD

38:22.758 --> 38:26.261
How about an afterparty at a karaoke bar?

38:27.095 --> 38:29.264
- That hurts.
- We should head back to the hotel.

38:29.348 --> 38:30.390
You want to do that?

38:30.974 --> 38:33.352
We'll just take a walk before we go.

38:33.435 --> 38:35.145
I want to take you somewhere.

38:35.437 --> 38:36.605
Where? Ouch!

38:37.397 --> 38:38.857
You're going to rip my side out!

38:38.941 --> 38:40.108
Okay, see you in Seoul.

38:40.192 --> 38:41.276
Okay, see you.

38:41.777 --> 38:43.320
- I'll text you. Bye.
- Bye.

38:43.445 --> 38:45.322
- Bye.
- Have a good night!

38:45.405 --> 38:46.406
You too!

38:48.826 --> 38:50.327
They look so good together.

38:51.078 --> 38:52.913
- Bye!
- Goodnight!

38:56.667 --> 39:00.420
- Bye! Drive safely!
- Bye!

39:04.091 --> 39:08.220
Shouldn't they be
in their honeymoon phase?

39:08.428 --> 39:09.721
But I feel like they'd go

39:10.097 --> 39:15.727
"Tilt your head to the right,
and I'll go the other way"

39:15.853 --> 39:18.146
when they kiss, right?

39:18.856 --> 39:21.066
Why? I think they look cute together.

39:21.608 --> 39:25.529
I haven't seen Ui-yeong so relaxed
around someone in forever.

39:26.530 --> 39:29.241
- And you know what Tae-seop said?
- Hmm?

39:29.366 --> 39:30.742
- I'm ready to pay.
- Okay.

39:30.826 --> 39:32.411
- We'll pay with this card.
- Okay.

39:36.290 --> 39:39.459
This is my first trip with Ui-yeong.

39:39.793 --> 39:42.129
I want to spend some time alone with her

39:42.296 --> 39:45.299
- so is it okay if we go on our own later?
- Sure.

39:46.091 --> 39:49.011
My heart skipped a beat, and I'm a man.

39:49.720 --> 39:51.638
That's a real man.

39:52.764 --> 39:55.100
- You think so?
- Yeah.

39:56.768 --> 39:57.811
Ready to go?

39:58.186 --> 40:00.188
- Shall we?
- Let's go!

40:04.818 --> 40:06.153
That's stunning.

40:06.236 --> 40:07.988
Is this where you wanted to come?

40:08.071 --> 40:09.114
I want to ride it!

40:10.490 --> 40:13.577
I knew it was a view spot,
but it's so tall.

40:14.536 --> 40:16.580
We don't need to get on it. We can just...

40:17.497 --> 40:18.498
look at it.

40:20.000 --> 40:23.921
You can see
the ocean and the city at once!

40:24.004 --> 40:25.213
That's so cool.

40:25.589 --> 40:27.841
Oh, you can see everything...

40:28.800 --> 40:33.013
It would've been awesome
if there were fireworks by the beach.

40:33.096 --> 40:36.183
There's always fireworks
at the beach, you know?

40:36.266 --> 40:38.018
Oh, right. Yeah.

40:42.105 --> 40:44.650
You've been a bit off since earlier.

40:44.733 --> 40:45.734
What do you mean?

40:46.234 --> 40:48.111
Are you scared?

40:49.112 --> 40:51.323
No, I'm not scared at all.

40:52.449 --> 40:53.992
Yeah, you are!

41:00.582 --> 41:01.917
- Here.
- Hmm?

41:03.794 --> 41:04.962
I'll hold your hands.

41:05.045 --> 41:06.296
Not scary anymore, right?

41:07.547 --> 41:08.590
I don't know...

41:08.674 --> 41:10.008
I guess it's not helping.

41:14.763 --> 41:17.057
Here. Just look at me.

41:18.850 --> 41:19.977
Not scary anymore, right?

41:25.148 --> 41:26.441
Not at all.

41:32.781 --> 41:34.700
- Look far away.
- Far away? Where?

41:34.783 --> 41:37.911
Over there. Not up. Look at the view.

41:46.169 --> 41:49.673
I didn't know
you'd booked a room for yourself.

41:51.842 --> 41:54.928
I thought you might be sharing a room
with Hyun-min.

41:58.432 --> 42:00.017
I guess I get it.

42:05.022 --> 42:06.273
It's so slow.

42:07.899 --> 42:08.942
Yeah.

42:12.154 --> 42:13.405
The door is opening.

42:14.781 --> 42:16.450
Goodnight. I'll call you later.

42:17.701 --> 42:18.702
Wait.

42:22.122 --> 42:24.082
Sure, I booked another room

42:24.291 --> 42:26.043
but I didn't say we'd sleep separately.

42:26.334 --> 42:27.377
What?

42:30.005 --> 42:31.048
Let's...

42:32.299 --> 42:33.592
stay together tonight.

43:41.785 --> 43:43.411
- Are you up?
- Yeah.

43:44.704 --> 43:46.748
We should get ready to leave now.

43:46.832 --> 43:48.750
No! I don't want to.

43:51.044 --> 43:52.379
Let's stay here for a bit more.

43:55.882 --> 43:56.883
Just a bit more.

43:59.594 --> 44:01.638
This is so nice.

44:04.307 --> 44:05.934
I really don't want to leave.

44:06.017 --> 44:08.979
- But we have to go.
- Okay, in just a bit!

44:36.464 --> 44:39.009
I'm heading down now.
I'll see you at the reception.

44:41.720 --> 44:42.721
Oh?

44:44.931 --> 44:46.183
Oh, gosh.

44:47.475 --> 44:49.019
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

44:50.228 --> 44:51.229
Huh?

44:51.313 --> 44:53.940
- Oh, it's all torn.
- Just a sec.

44:55.692 --> 44:57.569
Could I get a paper bag, please?

45:02.741 --> 45:03.742
Here you go, sir.

45:04.242 --> 45:05.785
Thank you.

45:05.869 --> 45:06.870
You're welcome.

45:08.413 --> 45:09.456
Hey, Ui-yeong.

45:12.751 --> 45:13.960
- Dad!
- Oh?

45:14.794 --> 45:16.880
Ui-yeong! What are you doing here?

45:17.547 --> 45:18.548
What?

45:18.798 --> 45:21.134
Your father?

45:21.676 --> 45:22.677
Yeah.

45:25.305 --> 45:26.306
Huh?

45:29.768 --> 45:31.645
LEE TAE-SUNG

45:32.020 --> 45:34.231
What brings you here?

45:34.314 --> 45:35.857
I thought you were in Gyeongju.

45:35.941 --> 45:39.110
Yeah, but there's a new line
being built to Sokcho.

45:39.194 --> 45:40.570
And I'm here for a workshop.

45:41.655 --> 45:44.449
So, are you two on a trip?

45:45.158 --> 45:46.326
No.

45:46.451 --> 45:49.663
I had to come here for work,
so he just tagged along.

45:50.789 --> 45:52.374
Who knew this would happen?

45:52.582 --> 45:54.542
I can't believe
I'm meeting your boyfriend.

45:55.627 --> 45:58.296
Well, I didn't bring him here to meet you.
It was a coincidence.

45:58.421 --> 45:59.589
Right.

45:59.839 --> 46:01.466
That's even more surprising.

46:01.716 --> 46:03.551
Maybe this is meant to be!

46:06.972 --> 46:12.018
Do you like Tae-seop
because he looks like me?

46:12.560 --> 46:13.687
- What?
- Just look!

46:13.770 --> 46:16.273
Tae-seop and Tae-sung.
Our names sound similar.

46:16.356 --> 46:17.691
We look alike, too.

46:17.774 --> 46:21.111
He has a small face with clear skin
and long limbs.

46:21.361 --> 46:23.655
He also has kind eyes, and...

46:23.738 --> 46:27.117
You really haven't changed a bit.

46:29.077 --> 46:30.453
Of course.

46:31.329 --> 46:34.249
Like the fact that you're my daughter,
no matter how old you become.

46:38.169 --> 46:40.422
I've been thinking a lot
about the old days lately.

46:40.880 --> 46:42.632
I missed a lot of important moments

46:42.882 --> 46:46.219
over trivial things in my life.

46:47.721 --> 46:50.724
I should've done everything
to stay with you and your mom.

46:54.769 --> 46:55.812
Hold on.

46:59.941 --> 47:02.110
- I'd better get going.
- Okay.

47:05.697 --> 47:07.699
- Take this.
- No, it's fine.

47:07.782 --> 47:10.452
- No, you sent me fruit, too. Here.
- No.

47:10.535 --> 47:11.786
It's fine.

47:13.330 --> 47:15.874
Use this to pay for gas

47:15.957 --> 47:17.917
and get Ui-yeong some chocolate,
her favorite.

47:20.503 --> 47:21.629
Let's meet more often.

47:22.339 --> 47:24.507
I'll really do my best.

47:27.093 --> 47:28.428
- Bye.
- Yeah.

47:29.304 --> 47:30.347
Goodbye, sir.

47:49.407 --> 47:50.492
Are you okay?

47:53.703 --> 47:54.829
It's so fascinating

47:55.830 --> 47:57.374
how uncomfortable I am

47:57.457 --> 48:01.252
yet my dad acts
like we've been close this whole time.

48:03.213 --> 48:06.966
He seems very cheerful and kind.

48:08.218 --> 48:09.594
He's always been like that.

48:10.845 --> 48:14.265
But maybe you only saw the best of him

48:14.682 --> 48:18.103
because we met him on his good day.

48:18.436 --> 48:19.479
I see.

48:20.271 --> 48:22.399
What's your mother like?

48:22.482 --> 48:23.942
- My mom?
- Yeah.

48:24.234 --> 48:25.735
She has quite the temper.

48:28.154 --> 48:31.241
She's rational,
always standing up for what's right

48:31.408 --> 48:33.159
and she's no easier on her family.

48:34.869 --> 48:37.497
They're really different.

48:37.997 --> 48:40.125
I see why it must've been hard
to live together.

48:41.751 --> 48:44.337
And I respect their decision.

48:48.049 --> 48:50.093
That was a really great trip,
all thanks to you.

48:50.635 --> 48:51.678
Same.

48:53.513 --> 48:55.723
I've traveled a lot for work

48:55.807 --> 49:00.603
but this is my first real vacation
in five or six years.

49:00.687 --> 49:03.064
I usually just do nothing at home.

49:03.148 --> 49:05.525
I'm not the type to travel around
by myself.

49:05.608 --> 49:06.609
I see.

49:07.819 --> 49:09.154
Five to six years ago?

49:13.491 --> 49:16.077
Who did you travel with then?

49:17.036 --> 49:20.457
Should we book the same days off
for the next vacation?

49:20.540 --> 49:21.958
Yeah, so who did you travel with?

49:22.041 --> 49:23.376
- Next month?
- Tell me.

49:23.460 --> 49:25.420
Tell me
who you went on your last trip with!

49:25.503 --> 49:26.880
Or maybe the month after?

49:28.882 --> 49:30.925
I'll let you off the hook today.

49:31.050 --> 49:32.135
Thanks.

50:03.666 --> 50:05.293
Are you going back to work tomorrow?

50:05.960 --> 50:07.754
Yeah, I am.

50:08.254 --> 50:12.133
But I'm extra sad to say goodbye
after spending so much time together.

50:13.676 --> 50:14.844
Hug me before you go, then.

50:19.599 --> 50:21.809
- That was so much fun.
- I don't want to go.

50:21.893 --> 50:23.937
- Let's go again soon.
- Okay.

50:28.525 --> 50:30.193
- Drive safely.
- Okay.

50:31.444 --> 50:32.529
Ui-yeong?

50:32.946 --> 50:34.030
Mom!

50:34.280 --> 50:35.281
"Mom"?

50:35.907 --> 50:38.409
You're kidding me.
First, Dad, and now, Mom?

50:38.701 --> 50:40.161
What's in the air today?

50:41.162 --> 50:42.330
Who are you?

50:45.333 --> 50:46.751
Mom, he's...

50:47.001 --> 50:49.420
He's my boyfriend.

50:50.505 --> 50:51.756
She's my mom.

50:51.881 --> 50:53.341
- Hello.
- Hello.

50:53.424 --> 50:54.676
He was just about to leave!

50:54.759 --> 50:56.427
- You should get going.
- What? But...

50:56.678 --> 50:58.888
- I can't just leave...
- You're busy! Go!

50:58.972 --> 51:00.515
- Hey...
- Go!

51:01.891 --> 51:02.976
Let's head in.

51:03.059 --> 51:04.602
- I'm exhausted.
- Goodbye.

51:04.686 --> 51:06.437
- Bye!
- Okay, bye.

51:06.521 --> 51:07.522
- Go!
- See you around.

51:07.605 --> 51:08.856
- Okay.
- Bye.

51:11.025 --> 51:12.026
Oh, gosh.

51:17.282 --> 51:18.741
I need to rest.

51:18.825 --> 51:20.243
So

51:21.119 --> 51:22.704
you've been seeing someone, huh?

51:24.372 --> 51:27.792
I met him on a blind date
and started dating him.

51:28.001 --> 51:29.127
It was pretty recent.

51:29.252 --> 51:32.589
I was going to tell you,
but you seemed busy.

51:32.672 --> 51:34.507
I didn't know if you were even curious.

51:34.591 --> 51:36.092
Why wouldn't I be curious?

51:36.217 --> 51:38.761
You chose him
after millions of blind dates.

51:39.846 --> 51:42.515
Don't tell me he's the carpoor guy.

51:43.766 --> 51:46.019
- Huh?
- Is he?

51:47.061 --> 51:51.107
Why couldn't you have found yourself
a proper guy?

51:51.190 --> 51:53.651
That was all a misunderstanding.

51:53.985 --> 51:55.862
Tae-seop isn't carpoor

51:56.321 --> 51:58.031
and he's really great.

51:59.616 --> 52:00.658
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

52:01.284 --> 52:03.953
Bring him home one day, then.
Let me meet him.

52:04.037 --> 52:05.496
Hmm? Why?

52:05.580 --> 52:07.957
I want to know why he even likes you

52:08.041 --> 52:10.877
and you know I have a good eye for people.

52:10.960 --> 52:11.961
You?

52:15.423 --> 52:17.634
You really want to meet him?

52:17.717 --> 52:21.179
Yeah, set a date and tell me. I'm serious.

52:22.472 --> 52:24.515
Okay, then.

52:25.391 --> 52:27.435
- I'm getting groceries.
- Okay.

52:34.192 --> 52:36.819
So, she wants me to bring you home.

52:37.362 --> 52:38.780
It's too much, right?

52:38.905 --> 52:41.115
No, I'm fine with that.

52:41.199 --> 52:44.494
I was so surprised earlier
that I couldn't introduce myself properly.

52:44.869 --> 52:48.956
And I'm sure it doesn't sit right with you
that I've only met your dad.

52:50.458 --> 52:52.752
Yeah, that's true.

52:53.294 --> 52:55.797
How about next Saturday, then?

52:55.880 --> 52:57.215
Sure, that sounds good.

52:57.298 --> 52:59.092
What does she like?

52:59.175 --> 53:00.635
My mom?

53:01.636 --> 53:02.804
Well...

53:03.221 --> 53:06.516
Her favorite thing is alcohol.

53:08.059 --> 53:09.060
Alcohol...

53:09.811 --> 53:12.855
So, why don't you buy
her second-favorite thing, flowers?

53:14.023 --> 53:16.526
Oh, yeah, I'll do that.

53:17.485 --> 53:19.320
- Thank you.
- Okay.

53:23.074 --> 53:24.117
Alcohol...

53:38.756 --> 53:44.971
SONG TAE-SEOP

53:46.556 --> 53:49.308
By the way, can you check inside your bag?

53:58.860 --> 54:02.655
I'm glad to have shared the time with you.
Let's love like the ocean.

54:12.165 --> 54:15.752
DINNER WITH MOM AND TAE-SEOP

54:18.546 --> 54:20.590
DINNER WITH MOM AND TAE-SEOP

54:25.344 --> 54:27.013
Welcome back, Ui-yeong.

54:27.096 --> 54:28.723
- Na-ri!
- Did you have a good break?

54:28.806 --> 54:31.100
Yeah, all thanks to your understanding.

54:32.059 --> 54:35.104
The gift set is all ready now

54:35.188 --> 54:37.940
and you can get updates on everything else
at the meeting.

54:38.024 --> 54:39.025
Okay.

54:40.026 --> 54:44.280
And you know I'm the team leader
while Mr. Oh is on probation, right?

54:45.281 --> 54:47.950
You can just call me Ms. Jung.

54:48.576 --> 54:50.453
- Let's work hard.
- Okay.

54:52.038 --> 54:53.372
Ms. Jung...

54:54.415 --> 54:56.918
Hey, Na-ri!
Are those prescription glasses?

54:57.210 --> 54:58.544
Of course, they are.

54:58.711 --> 54:59.837
Let's work hard, okay?

55:07.804 --> 55:11.474
She seems to be really enjoying her time
as a temporary team leader.

55:16.395 --> 55:19.357
Hmm? Is something bothering you?

55:19.857 --> 55:21.234
Why the long face?

55:22.235 --> 55:27.073
My mom accidentally saw me with Tae-seop.

55:27.740 --> 55:29.826
Now, she wants me to invite him
to our house.

55:30.952 --> 55:34.121
Don't all parents do that?
Maybe she really likes him.

55:34.413 --> 55:37.291
Yeah, all parents do that, but not my mom.

55:38.000 --> 55:39.293
It's so odd.

55:42.964 --> 55:44.006
What's going on?

55:52.348 --> 55:53.891
Ms. Park Jeong-im.

55:53.975 --> 55:55.059
Oh, here.

56:00.273 --> 56:02.191
I got a health check-up done

56:02.650 --> 56:06.529
and the MRA showed
signs of a cerebral aneurysm.

56:08.948 --> 56:11.784
Do you get headaches or dizzy often?

56:11.868 --> 56:15.997
No, nothing noticeable.

56:16.080 --> 56:17.623
I also have no family history of it.

56:17.707 --> 56:20.126
It's more common for them
to be asymptomatic.

56:20.209 --> 56:22.753
Some discover them
through check-ups, like you

56:22.837 --> 56:25.590
and others discover them
when they rupture and cause a hemorrhage.

56:25.715 --> 56:26.757
Cerebral hemorrhage?

56:27.216 --> 56:28.384
Just in the worst case.

56:28.467 --> 56:30.887
Its risk depends
on the size and the location

56:30.970 --> 56:32.513
so let's do a detailed check-up.

56:32.889 --> 56:35.057
Try to sleep well for the next few days

56:35.433 --> 56:38.561
and stay away from alcohol, smoking,
and stressful environments.

56:38.644 --> 56:39.645
Okay.

56:46.444 --> 56:48.696
Jeong-im?

56:50.406 --> 56:52.033
- Jeong-im!
- Yeah.

56:52.408 --> 56:54.702
Did you go to the doctor? What did he say?

56:54.785 --> 56:57.496
He wants me to get some further testing.

56:58.623 --> 56:59.624
Oh, gosh.

57:01.292 --> 57:02.752
Have you told your daughter yet?

57:03.252 --> 57:04.253
Not yet.

57:04.754 --> 57:07.381
I'll tell her once I'm sure of it
after the check-up.

57:08.007 --> 57:11.260
And I'm seeing her boyfriend this weekend.

57:11.469 --> 57:13.012
Is she seeing someone?

57:13.095 --> 57:14.764
After all those blind dates!

57:14.847 --> 57:17.266
I caught the two hugging.

57:19.769 --> 57:20.811
You know

57:21.145 --> 57:24.315
I just invited him for a meal
to see if he was a good guy.

57:25.191 --> 57:28.694
You need to tell her soon.
She'll be so shocked to hear it later.

57:28.861 --> 57:30.404
You're covered by insurance.

57:30.571 --> 57:34.325
It's not about the money.
I just don't want to worry her.

57:34.533 --> 57:36.369
If I weren't alone

57:36.452 --> 57:39.372
she wouldn't have had to bear
the worry alone.

57:40.539 --> 57:42.291
Are you not going to tell your husband?

57:44.293 --> 57:45.836
What? My husband?

57:47.004 --> 57:50.341
We've lived apart for 20 years.
I'd rather fight whatever this is alone.

57:50.675 --> 57:53.010
There's no way I'm asking him for help.

57:54.553 --> 57:56.722
Yeah, that makes more sense.

58:13.823 --> 58:18.244
Is this a sauna or what?
Everyone's sighing

58:18.327 --> 58:21.205
and the air feels so gloomy.

58:21.288 --> 58:24.750
I'm meeting Ui-yeong's mother
this weekend.

58:24.834 --> 58:28.129
You guys are that serious already?
That's so fast!

58:28.462 --> 58:33.718
You want my secret that stole
my mother-in-law's heart?

58:34.218 --> 58:35.219
What?

58:35.761 --> 58:39.223
It's like a blind date, but different.

58:39.306 --> 58:41.017
It's not about impressing her.

58:41.100 --> 58:43.894
It's about the actions you make
to show that you're trying.

58:44.061 --> 58:45.521
- Actions...
- Mother-in-laws love

58:45.604 --> 58:47.648
seeing their son-in-laws
trying to impress them.

58:48.524 --> 58:51.569
I got flowers, her favorite,
and planned my outfit.

58:51.652 --> 58:52.737
Okay, here's what you do.

58:53.195 --> 58:56.365
"I prepared flowers
because I heard you love them

58:56.657 --> 58:59.118
and tried to dress up for the occasion.
Is this okay?"

58:59.201 --> 59:00.703
That's what you say, okay?

59:00.953 --> 59:02.913
Shouldn't I sound more confident?

59:02.997 --> 59:05.166
No, listen. "I prepared flowers for you

59:05.249 --> 59:07.084
and dressed up today. Do I look okay?"

59:07.168 --> 59:08.669
That doesn't sound human enough.

59:08.753 --> 59:11.338
You have to make it really clear
that you're making an effort.

59:11.422 --> 59:13.257
- You really don't get it. Next.
- Got it.

59:13.466 --> 59:15.885
Oh, my liver isn't ready.

59:15.968 --> 59:17.386
Apparently, she loves to drink.

59:18.095 --> 59:21.223
You should take
at least two hangover pills before you go.

59:21.557 --> 59:22.767
- Two?
- Yeah.

59:22.933 --> 59:25.227
Even if you get tipsy,
try not to act like it.

59:25.311 --> 59:27.813
And show enthusiastic reactions
whenever she talks.

59:27.897 --> 59:31.650
Answer her loud and clear.
Don't get too shy.

59:32.651 --> 59:34.236
- Loud and clear.
- Blink your eyes

59:34.403 --> 59:35.738
and go, "Yes!"

59:35.821 --> 59:37.823
- I'm not sure about that.
- Yeah, that was bad.

59:40.493 --> 59:41.619
Alright.

59:51.754 --> 59:53.547
My gosh.

59:54.090 --> 59:55.758
Can you do that more regularly?

59:56.675 --> 59:59.553
It's like you're trying
to rip the floor up.

01:00:00.596 --> 01:00:01.972
Come on.

01:00:03.390 --> 01:00:04.725
Goodness.

01:00:15.986 --> 01:00:19.281
Why are you putting everything away?
We use them!

01:00:19.615 --> 01:00:22.660
It needs to be a bit messy
to feel like a home.

01:00:22.743 --> 01:00:24.870
But we don't need to show that today.

01:00:25.162 --> 01:00:27.081
- Huh?
- And Mom

01:00:27.164 --> 01:00:29.583
don't ask him uncomfortable questions,
alright?

01:00:29.667 --> 01:00:32.294
And try not to sound too cold.

01:00:32.378 --> 01:00:34.880
Try to be nice and friendly, okay?

01:00:36.423 --> 01:00:37.591
- Happy now?
- Yeah.

01:00:38.467 --> 01:00:40.136
Good for someone who never smiles.

01:00:41.804 --> 01:00:44.348
Mom! Why is there no rice?

01:00:45.182 --> 01:00:48.185
It'd be poor hospitality
if I cooked the lunch myself.

01:00:48.269 --> 01:00:50.396
- I know what to eat.
- What?

01:00:52.982 --> 01:00:54.233
Oh, I'd better order it now.

01:00:54.692 --> 01:00:56.819
- Is he allergic to anything?
- No, he's not.

01:00:56.902 --> 01:00:59.113
- I'm getting eobokjaengban, then.
- Okay.

01:00:59.530 --> 01:01:02.741
- Where's my phone?
- I told you to put the towel away!

01:01:03.075 --> 01:01:04.243
Seriously.

01:01:04.326 --> 01:01:05.786
And the water!

01:01:07.830 --> 01:01:10.207
Oh! I have to get rid of the drinks.

01:01:30.644 --> 01:01:31.812
Oh, right.

01:01:48.996 --> 01:01:50.956
Huh? He's early.

01:01:51.081 --> 01:01:52.917
Mom! I think Tae-seop's here!

01:01:53.083 --> 01:01:54.084
Coming!

01:02:01.342 --> 01:02:02.843
Dad?

01:02:06.805 --> 01:02:08.015
Hi, Ui-yeong.

01:02:16.523 --> 01:02:17.733
Alright.

01:02:24.490 --> 01:02:26.283
It's been a minute.

01:02:45.636 --> 01:02:46.679
Ui-yeong.

01:02:48.639 --> 01:02:49.723
Tae-seop.

01:02:50.349 --> 01:02:52.434
Oh, you're here!

01:02:53.519 --> 01:02:55.354
- Come in.
- Yes, sir.

01:03:00.442 --> 01:03:01.568
- Hello.
- Hello.

01:03:01.652 --> 01:03:03.445
We keep running into each other.

01:03:03.529 --> 01:03:06.824
It seems like you're meant to be around
for a long time.

01:03:38.397 --> 01:03:41.191
THE PRACTICAL GUIDE TO LOVE

01:03:47.906 --> 01:03:50.909
A DATE WITH TAE-SEOP

01:04:00.711 --> 01:04:04.006
LET'S LOVE LIKE THE OCEAN

01:04:08.761 --> 01:04:12.306
LET'S STAY TOGETHER TONIGHT

01:04:14.266 --> 01:04:16.393
That wasn't just for you to meet Tae-seop.

01:04:16.602 --> 01:04:18.395
It was also for him to get to know you.

01:04:19.271 --> 01:04:20.773
I'm really fine.

01:04:20.981 --> 01:04:22.524
Today was just not meant to be.

01:04:23.067 --> 01:04:24.985
Why don't you stay here for a while?

01:04:25.944 --> 01:04:28.739
Ui-yeong! Why is he driving you to work?

01:04:29.281 --> 01:04:30.282
Ji-su.

01:04:30.449 --> 01:04:32.576
How do you two know each other?

01:04:33.035 --> 01:04:35.287
Are you out right now?

01:04:35.621 --> 01:04:36.872
What misunderstanding?

01:04:38.040 --> 01:04:39.041
Mom!

01:04:39.500 --> 01:04:41.168
- Mom!
- She...

01:04:42.252 --> 01:04:43.587
fainted in the lobby.

01:04:44.296 --> 01:04:45.672
It's all my fault.

01:04:50.844 --> 01:04:52.846
Subtitles by: Min-sun Kim
